The ranking method follows Aider's repository map:
https://aider.chat/2023/10/22/repomap.html
Aider is licensed under Apache-2.0. No Aider source code or query text is
included in symapper. The tree-sitter queries in queries/ are original.

The ranking uses PageRank (Page, Brin, Motwani, Winograd, "The PageRank
Citation Ranking: Bringing Order to the Web", Stanford InfoLab, 1999) with a
personalization vector as in Haveliwala, "Topic-Sensitive PageRank", WWW 2002.

Parsing uses tree-sitter and the following grammar crates, linked as
dependencies. Each is distributed under its own MIT license:
- tree-sitter: https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter
- tree-sitter-typescript (TypeScript and TSX):
  https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-typescript
- tree-sitter-javascript (JavaScript and JSX):
  https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-javascript
- tree-sitter-python: https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-python
- tree-sitter-go: https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-go
- tree-sitter-rust: https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-rust
- tree-sitter-swift: https://github.com/alex-pinkus/tree-sitter-swift

The full list of linked third-party crates, with their license texts, is in
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.

